import json,subprocess
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).parent
common='''

## 14 November2026 — accepted shared-search direction and bounded pilot

Bill approved the holistic assessment, instructed updating existing stories, creating gaps, and proceeding with a small live Wiki/GEMP/SCOMPLINK pilot covering symbols, uniqueness and decklists containing a card. He explicitly authorizes first-principles judgment, including contradicting earlier assumptions where useful. [Assessment](https://github.com/swccg-guild/work/blob/main/evidence/435/search-design/search-and-display.md).

**Guiding principles:** optimize trustworthy answers and the user's job; share identities and public card-filter meanings rather than forcing all screens, defaults, data ownership or private filters to match. Preserve catalog/publication/text-state identity, provenance and unknowns. Distinguish release product, printed symbol and a symbol referenced in game text. The same public query over the same snapshot/scope should match; genuinely different scopes should be explicit. Faithful symbols and searchable/copyable semantic text can coexist.

**Implementation split:** [449](https://github.com/swccg-guild/work/issues/449) owns the small cross-system live pilot; [450](https://github.com/swccg-guild/work/issues/450) owns connected Wiki discovery beyond cards; [451](https://github.com/swccg-guild/work/issues/451) owns GEMP Current deck/My decks scopes. Existing32 remains the full public card-filter rollout,33 the shared public deck library,87 format search,173 deck-display research,435 symbol assets/meaning. No duplicate full deck database/index or upstream-PC deployment is planned. Full-story ownership/status is not silently changed by this pilot.

**Pilot defaults chosen under Bill's authorization:** use a clearly bounded public snapshot and three native entry points; our own labeled SCOMPLINK pilot, not the PC production service. Keep Wiki broad-search navigation, GEMP's selected play context and existing editing flow, and a quick SCOMPLINK lookup. Common queries cover symbol identity/aliases/roles, typed uniqueness, and real deck membership/counts. No hidden game state or private saved decks enter the public snapshot. Role/type/unknown/empty cases and native regressions are acceptance tests.

**Acceptance addition for this story:** consume or interoperate with449's pinned query/data contract, preserve context/date/version identities and source links, and retain a concrete coverage/gap ledger. The pilot does not by itself satisfy this story's full rollout AC. Archive.org hold remains absolute; metadata/backups may proceed but no request, capture or preservation-completion claim is allowed.
'''
specific={32:'For full32, public card-metadata filter parity is the goal; GEMP-private collection controls and exports/actions need context-appropriate behavior, not identical widgets. Source authority is a shared catalog with explicit field provenance, not an assumption that engine data describes every historical printing. Preserve existing basic/advanced/export capabilities while testing improvements. Existing open questions are retained historically; the pilot choices above resolve its bounded scope without blocking on a future public hostname or full rollout decision.',33:'For33, model deck occurrence/revision, counted entries, exact versus family identity, actual zones/setup roles, player/event/format/date/source and completeness. An incomplete list cannot prove a card absent. Reuse existing Wiki records/downloads as sources; starting cards displayed separately must not be counted again. Keep as-played history separate from a modern compatible import and surface unsupported mappings.',87:'For87, format-search output should use the same format/card identities and explicit text/date context as449 and32. A card existing in the catalog, being format-legal and being implemented are separate facts. Keep the LOTR-format UI benefits without assuming Wiki histories come from the engine alone.',435:'For435, the previous A/B/C question is superseded as a permanent either/or decision. One semantic representation should generate faithful symbol display, readable text and useful copy/search text.449 will test results across display modes before broader435 rollout. The already merged CardMaker shared exporter remains the artwork source; do not infer regular/AI rings or historical marks from filenames or a generic style label.',173:'For173, retain research/display ownership and references;449 implements the newly authorized bounded search pilot,33 owns public deck data and451 owns native current/saved-deck scope. The research-only restrictions of173 do not become a hidden permission blocker for the separately authorized449 implementation.'}
